WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.640
Have you ever wondered

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:06.560
if there are more natural ways
to lower your high blood pressure,

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.520
guard against Alzheimer's,
lose weight, and feel better?

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.720
Well, it turns out there is!

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.200
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.560
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:24.480
Today, we look at boosting our GLP-1
the way mother nature intended.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.160
Plant-predominant diets may play
a "major role in reversing

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.720
the obesity
and chronic disease epidemics,"

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.640
just as plant-based
dietary interventions

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.880
may arrest or even reverse
type 2 diabetes

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.920
and cardiovascular disease
on an individual basis.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.120
In a previous video,

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.520
I showed how a tofu burger
boosted levels

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.840
of the appetite-suppressing
hormone GLP-1

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.040
higher than a meat burger

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.120
in both people with diabetes
and without,

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:48.720
even though the two burgers
were matched

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.720
for calories
and macronutrients.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.280
One thing may have given
the plant-based meal an edge,

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:56.720
though, at least over time:
increased fiber.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:00.160
The bacterial fermentation
of dietary fibers in the colon

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:04.960
produces short-chain fatty acids
called acetate, propionate,

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:09.280
and butyrate, which, in turn,
stimulate release of GLP-1.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:12.160
In this way, prebiotics,
like dietary fiber,

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:13.680
represent
an alternative strategy

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.560
for boosting production
of GLP-1.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:19.280
In contrast, a bacterial
breakdown product of tryptophan,

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:20.960
which is concentrated
in animal protein,

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:22.720
has been found
to have opposite effects

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.200
on GLP-1 release.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.480
How do we know fiber-derived
short-chain fatty acids

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:30.320
boost GLP-1 in the first place?

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:33.440
Well, all three circulating
short-chain fatty acids

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:36.160
were associated with
higher GLP-1 concentrations

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:37.200
in the blood,

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.440
but that doesn’t prove
cause-and-effect.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:43.760
For that, you need to stick
tubes in people’s butts.

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:46.080
Getting a rectal infusion
of acetate

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.720
indeed causes GLP-1 levels
to go up.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.120
And the amount of acetate
concentrations in the blood

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:55.120
reached after rectal infusion
were within an achievable range,

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:56.480
in the ballpark
of what you’d get

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:59.360
eating 15 or more grams
of fiber a day,

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:02.640
here in the form
of oat bran cereal and muffins.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.880
There’s a third way
to get appetite-suppressing

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:07.200
short-chain fatty acids
in our bloodstream

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:10.080
besides the top-down approach
of eating healthy food

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:11.600
and the bottoms-up approach

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.120
of getting them squirted
in your tush.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.520
When you consume vinegar,

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:21.401
its acetic acid is rapidly
neutralized into acetate.

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:23.760
No wonder vinegar
has evidently been used

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:26.400
to treat obesity for centuries.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.200
Does this all translate
into reducing cravings,

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.440
eating less,
and losing weight?

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.480
Let’s scan people’s brains
and find out.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:35.880
Researchers delivered
propionate,

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:38.000
a fiber-derived,
short-chain fatty acid,

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.320
into the colons
of study participants

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:44.800
while showing them images of
pizza, cakes, and chocolates,

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:47.360
and found that increasing
colonic propionate

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:48.880
seemed to reduce
brain activation

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:51.120
in the reward centers
of the brain.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.680
This was accompanied by
a decrease in subjective appeal

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:56.480
of these kinds of foods,
they didn’t look as tasty,

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:59.280
and this translated
into reduced caloric intake

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.360
at a buffet meal.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.200
Note that this effect
didn’t seem to correlate

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.640
with GLP-1 changes, though;

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:06.800
so, it’s possible
that short-chain fatty acids

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:09.600
produced in the colon
are accessing the brain directly

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:12.160
and reducing appetite
some other way.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:14.400
Regardless,
does the boost in GLP-1

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.480
and the short-term reduction
of caloric intake

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:19.360
from the direct delivery
of propionate to the colon

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.280
translate into
better weight control

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:22.960
in overweight adults?

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:26.480
Yes, long-term colonic
propionate delivery

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:29.680
prevents body weight gain,
particularly deep abdominal fat,

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.040
and may even reduce liver fat

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:32.960
in those with
fatty liver disease.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:36.880
So, you’d expect prebiotic
trials to show the same,

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:38.400
and sometimes they worked,

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.280
boosting GLP-1
and driving down hunger,

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.240
but overall, human interventions
with prebiotics

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:46.640
have shown mixed results.

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:48.480
And that’s putting it lightly.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:52.160
Effects on GLP-1 appear
to be highly contradictory,

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:56.320
with different isolated dietary
fibers bumping GLP-1 up,

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:59.520
some dropping it down,
and others having no effect.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:02.400
In some cases, it’s possible
that macronutrients

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.400
that would otherwise
stimulate GLP-1

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.800
might get caught up
in viscous, fibrous masses

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.160
and result in lower levels.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:11.920
Regardless, results for
short-term prebiotic trials

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:14.400
are said to be
"completely inconclusive"

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.720
for GLP-1.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:18.480
One problem may be the dose.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:19.040
For example, in this study,

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:21.120
researchers tested
refined-grain bread

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:22.360
versus whole-grain bread,

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:24.800
and although the whole-grain
bread improved satiety,

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:27.120
it had no effect on GLP-1.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:30.640
The difference in fiber content
was only about five grams,

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:33.200
though, which may not be enough.

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:34.800
In this study,
study participants

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.880
were randomized
to get either 5 or 10 grams

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:39.120
of a fiber supplement
called Fibersol,

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:42.080
and the five-gram dose appeared
to have no greater effect

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:43.760
on GLP-1 than placebo.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:47.360
Only the 10-gram dose worked,
which is about two tablespoons.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:49.920
Similarly, there were
significant delays in hunger

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:53.600
and increased satiety
after 10 grams, but not five.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.800
And studies like this
may only last a few hours.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.360
The more fiber-rich foods
you eat,

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.280
the more you foster the growth
of more fiber-feeders,

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:07.120
which means even more
GLP-1 secretion over time.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:10.000
Eating more fiber-rich foods
may eventually even promote

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.240
the emergence of more
GLP-1 secreting cells

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:14.160
in our intestinal lining.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:15.520
Check out this study.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:17.520
Adaptation
of colonic fermentation

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:20.160
and GLP-1 secretion with
increased wheat fiber intake

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.680
for not a few hours
but an entire year.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:26.320
People who eat whole grains
tend to get less diabetes,

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:28.720
but even if you switch to
whole wheat for weeks or months,

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:30.240
there doesn’t seem
to be much improvement

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:32.080
in blood sugar control.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.240
It turns out
it may take longer than that

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:38.320
for our colon to adapt
to the increased fiber intake.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:41.360
Colonic adaptation
to increased wheat fiber intake

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:44.160
takes many months
but eventually results

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:46.400
in increased
short fatty acid production

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:48.480
and GLP-1 secretion.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.400
This was found
when people were randomized

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:53.840
to a year of either All Bran
or Rice Krispies cereal

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:54.800
for breakfast.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:57.040
And there was
a significant increase

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:58.640
in short-chain
fatty acid production

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:01.280
and GLP-1 secretion
in the higher-fiber group,

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:06.000
but it took 9 to 12 months
for these benefits to develop.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.240
And finally,
people may not understand

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:10.240
the complexity of dietary fiber,

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:12.400
thinking that
it’s a single nutrient,

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:15.120
but there are literally
thousands of types of fiber

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:16.000
in plant foods,

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.320
and each one may support
different communities

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:20.400
of bacteria in our gut.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.400
That’s the reasoning
behind recommendations

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:25.520
that people take
a "50-food challenge,"

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:28.080
eating at least 50
different plant foods a week

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:30.800
to achieve a diet
diverse enough

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:33.760
to feed a vast spectrum
of bacteria.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:35.520
Those who get more fiber
in their diet

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:38.640
are significantly less likely
to get heart disease,

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:40.240
and die from heart disease.

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:42.480
Less likely to get
cardiovascular disease

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:44.880
in general, and less likely
to die from it.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.320
Less likely to have a stroke,

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:49.280
less likely to get diabetes
and colorectal cancer,

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:51.760
less likely to die
from cancer across the board,

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:55.040
and less likely to die
from all causes put together.

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:59.520
But all of this
is for fiber from food.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:01.920
In terms of fiber intake
for optimal health,

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.160
the first line of defense
for disease prevention

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:08.160
is to focus on fiber from foods
rather than supplements.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:09.440
For the treatment of disease,

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:11.280
there is a lack
of evidence-based research

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:15.280
to support the use
of most isolated fiber types.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:18.240
Take that supplement Fibersol,
for example.

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:20.240
Fibersol is
a registered trademark

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:23.040
of the Matsutani
Chemical Industry Company,

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.200
the one who invented it.

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:27.120
"Looking to increase
the fiber content

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:28.720
of a finished product?

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:31.920
Check out
our innovation success stories."

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:35.920
Eat your donut cookie
whipped cream milkshake,

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:38.240
it’s got fiber!

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:39.920
Maybe better to stick to foods

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:43.920
that were invented instead
by Mother Nature.

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:46.160
The majority of cells
producing GLP-1

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:47.920
are located
at the end of the gut,

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:49.680
in our large intestine.

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:52.080
But prebiotics
don’t represent the only

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:54.720
"slow digestion-oriented
dietary strategy"

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:57.600
to sustain
the secretion of GLP-1.

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:00.240
Prebiotics can be used
to promote metabolic health

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:04.000
and longevity by stimulating
intestinal production of GLP-1,

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:07.360
and so too
can the drug Acarbose,

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:09.200
which acts as a starch blocker,

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:11.680
inhibiting the enzymes
that would normally digest

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:14.800
carbohydrates earlier
in the small intestine.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:17.760
Acarbose-induced transfer
of carbs to the lower parts

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:20.880
of the intestine
increases GLP-1 levels.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:23.840
And since changes in GLP-1
correlate with weight loss

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:25.120
in those on the drug,

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:28.160
it’s reasonable to suspect
that GLP-1 is a mediator

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:30.800
of the favorable impact
of acarbose therapy

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:32.720
on weight control.

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:37.120
There’s also a third strategy,
eating "lente" carbohydrates,

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:39.760
from the Latin lentus for slow.

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:43.920
Instead of taking a drug to slow
dietary carbohydrate digestion,

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:45.680
what about just choosing a diet

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:48.880
centered around slow-digesting
"lente" carbohydrates

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.880
to achieve comparable benefits?

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:52.480
That’s the theory, anyway.

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:55.120
So, that means pasta,
beans, groats,

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:57.760
meaning structurally intact
grain kernels,

00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:59.600
as well as sprouted grains.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:01.200
Let’s start with beans.

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:03.600
Here, researchers found
enhanced secretion

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.600
of satiety-promoting
gut hormones

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:07.680
after the consumption
of white bread

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:11.600
that had been enriched with
coarsely ground chickpea flour,

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:13.520
and the more chickpea
it contained,

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:16.320
the higher
the GLP-1 levels spiked,

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:18.320
but where are you going
to find chickpea bread?

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:20.880
What about just eating beans?

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:23.120
Asking people to eat five cups
(850-900 g) of beans a week

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:25.040
spontaneously led
to health benefits

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:26.720
similar to those seen
after asking people

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:30.000
to cut 500 calories
out of their daily diet,

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.280
but there was no change
in GLP-1 levels.

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:35.360
What about cocoa beans?

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:38.080
I wish, but sadly,
no effect of dark chocolate

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:40.000
on GLP-1 either.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:44.000
The one pasta study I could find
also failed to bump GLP-1,

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:46.480
but the one
sprouted grain study I found

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:49.600
showed higher GLP-1 response
to sprouted bread,

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:51.440
compared to four other types
of bread,

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:54.080
which didn’t differ
significantly from each other.

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:55.680
Eleven- or 12-grain bread

00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:57.840
was no different
than white bread?

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:00.080
That’s what’s generally found
when comparing products

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:03.280
made with whole-grain flour
to refined-grain flour;

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:05.920
there aren’t any immediate
right-after-the-meal effects

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:08.720
of whole wheat bread compared
to white bread, for example.

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:09.920
You can’t just eat bread

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:13.200
and expect some kind
of "doughzempic" effect,

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:15.680
because, as I explained
in my last few videos,

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:19.760
food structure is critical
for optimal health.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:21.840
When grains are milled
into flour,

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:23.760
whether whole wheat or white,

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:26.800
their cell walls are ruptured
and the starch spills out

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:28.560
and never makes it
down to our colon;

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:30.640
so, we don’t get
their added benefit.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:31.680
This is one of the reasons

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:34.560
former Harvard nutrition chair
Walt Willett

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:37.200
has argued that the term
whole grain

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:42.160
should probably be reserved for
only whole intact grain kernels,

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:46.240
otherwise known as groats,
the "wholiest" of grains.

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:49.840
In my book How Not to Diet,
I talk about my BROL bowl,

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:52.400
a prebiotic mix
that includes barley groats,

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:54.240
rye groats, and oat groats.

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:57.520
What effect might they have
on GLP-1?

00:10:57.520 --> 00:10:59.120
If you give people bread

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:02.400
containing some
whole intact barley groats,

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:04.800
there’s no immediate difference
in GLP-1 levels

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:06.320
in the subsequent three hours,

00:11:06.320 --> 00:11:08.560
but the groats
wouldn’t even have had time

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.800
to make it down to your colon
that quickly.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:12.640
However,
after your good bacteria

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:15.200
have had a chance
to break open their cell walls,

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:17.920
you get a greater,
higher GLP-1 bump

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:22.960
more than 12 hours later,
at breakfast the next day.

00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:23.680
The question, though,

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:26.960
is whether that translates
into a suppressed appetite.

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:30.800
And indeed, lower food intake
not just at breakfast,

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:35.200
but also at lunch the next day,
14 hours later!

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:38.080
Having barley kernels
at an evening meal

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:40.320
not only increased GLP-1
the next day,

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:43.200
boosting blood levels
by 43 percent at breakfast,

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:44.960
but feelings of hunger
decreased

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:46.320
during the entire next day,

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:48.960
and the research participants
ate about 100 fewer calories

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:51.120
of an all-you-can-eat lunch,

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:53.360
just because they had
some barley groats

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:55.680
fourteen hours before.

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:57.680
Eat barley groats
three days in row

00:11:57.680 --> 00:12:00.800
and on the fourth day
see a 56 percent increase

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:04.080
in the level of GLP-1
in your blood.

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:05.920
What about rye groats?

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:08.640
Eat rye groats for supper,
and more than 10 hours later,

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:12.880
your GLP-1 levels are up,
and your appetite is down.

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:14.240
Researchers found
that participants

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:16.400
had an increased
subjective feeling of satiety

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:18.880
during the course
of the entire next day.

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:21.440
So, rye groats
"demonstrate anti-diabetes

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:22.800
and anti-obesity potential

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:25.200
as manifested by
enhanced blood sugar control

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:26.720
and increased GLP-1

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:29.520
and the accompanying
appetite suppression."

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:30.560
And there was a correlation

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:32.000
between the short-chain
fatty acids,

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:34.800
acetate and propionate,
and GLP-1 response,

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:35.920
suggesting that, indeed,

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:38.560
we may have
our good gut bugs to thank

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:40.960
for the beneficial effects.

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:41.920
The cells that produce

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:43.800
the appetite-suppressing
hormone GLP-1

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:45.760
in response to calorie exposure

00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:47.440
are concentrated
all the way down

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:49.680
at the end
of our digestive tract,

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:50.880
which is why our appetites

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:53.680
are not suppressed very much
these days.

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:55.280
The majority
of the calories we eat

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:57.600
are absorbed early
in our digestive tract;

00:12:57.600 --> 00:12:59.920
so, they never make it down
far enough.

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:02.880
When we eat a donut,
its fat, sugar, and starch

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:04.800
get absorbed quickly, high up,

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:06.800
before reaching the part
of our digestive tract

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:08.560
where we produce
most of the hormone

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:10.400
that suppresses our appetite.

00:13:10.400 --> 00:13:12.960
So, from a GLP-1 standpoint,

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:15.520
it’s like we never ate
much of anything.

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:17.840
No wonder we reach for donut #2.

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:23.520
How can we eat a donut
and still get GLP-1 activation?

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:24.720
Surgery!

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:26.880
Bariatric surgery
can involve cutting out

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:28.720
part of our small intestine

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:30.160
so some of the donut calories

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:33.200
may reach the end of it
after all.

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:36.640
What if you want to eat a donut,
still get GLP-1 activation,

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:39.280
and keep your anatomy intact?

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:40.320
Drugs!

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:43.200
By injecting GLP-1
mimicking drugs, like Ozempic,

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:46.400
you can get GLP-1 activation
no matter what you eat.

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:49.360
You could also take
the starch-blocker drug acarbose

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:51.600
to slow the digestion
of carbohydrates,

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:56.240
or the fat-blocker drug orlistat
to slow the digestion of fats.

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:58.400
But what if you want
GLP-1 activation

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:00.560
without drugs or surgery?

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:04.240
Well, you could try
not eating donuts.

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:06.160
Ancestral humans
might have consumed

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:08.720
as much as 100 grams
of fiber daily.

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:10.640
That’s about six times

00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:12.560
what most of us are getting
these days.

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:15.360
We evolved eating massive
amounts of whole plant foods,

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:17.680
the only place
fiber is found in abundance.

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:19.680
So, by eating
the way nature intended,

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:22.800
we can release GLP-1
the way nature intended,

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:25.760
which helps explain why
a whole food, plant-based diet

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:28.080
is one of the most powerful
weight loss interventions

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:30.240
ever published.

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:33.040
But what do we do
about our cravings?

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:34.880
What are some
therapeutic approaches

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:35.760
to addressing them?

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:37.360
Well, there are drugs,
of course,

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:39.680
but in terms
of food-based interventions,

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:41.840
there are thylakoids,

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:44.080
which are just the
chlorophyll-rich membranes

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:47.280
inside leaves where
photosynthesis takes place.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:49.600
Thylakoids act as fat blockers,

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:51.440
delaying our digestion of fats

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:55.840
and promoting the release
of satiety hormones like GLP-1.

00:14:55.840 --> 00:14:57.600
When we eat thylakoids,

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:00.160
in other words, when we bite
into a leaf of spinach,

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:01.200
for instance,

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:03.600
the thylakoid membranes
are able to resist

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:05.360
our digestive enzymes.

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:06.960
They can last for hours
in our gut

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:08.640
before finally
being broken down,

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:12.320
and it is in those hours
when they work their magic.

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:15.200
Thylakoids glom
onto tiny droplets of fat

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:17.440
in our digestive tract,
and, in this way,

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:20.480
powerfully slow our digestion
of fat.

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:22.720
And that means more GLP-1.

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:25.680
Yes, GLP-1 is a hormone
that is being developed

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:27.600
as an anti-obesity drug

00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:30.000
(this was published two years
before Ozempic).

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.480
But thylakoids
can cause our natural,

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:34.320
endogenous release of GLP-1,

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:36.400
which is an easier
and more physiological way

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:37.920
to enhance GLP-1 levels

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:40.720
to achieve satiety
and calorie balance.

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:43.920
But does it
actually cut cravings?

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:47.680
Spinach extracts
were disguised in jam and juice

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:51.120
to sneak thylakoids
undetected into meals,

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:53.600
and those unwittingly eating
the equivalent

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:55.760
of about half a cup (100 g)
of cooked spinach

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:57.600
felt significantly less hungry

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:00.640
and more satiated
over the next few hours.

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:03.840
Give someone the equivalent
of a shot of wheatgrass juice

00:16:03.840 --> 00:16:06.160
or what they might get
in a "green drink"

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:07.520
or green smoothie,

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:10.240
and not only do they feel
more satiated,

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:14.480
but their cravings for sweet,
salty, and fatty snacks,

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:17.120
such as potato chips,
chocolate, and cinnamon buns,

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:19.120
drop by about a third.

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.640
Feed them candy anyway,

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:24.080
and those who unknowingly
had been snuck some spinach,

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:27.920
report liking the sweets
significantly less.

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:30.480
The satiating power of greens
has been attributed

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:32.160
to their high fiber
and water contents

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:33.360
and low calorie density,

00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:36.560
but the thylakoids
may be their secret weapon,

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:39.280
presumably because of
the increased release of GLP-1

00:16:39.280 --> 00:16:41.920
following
thylakoid supplementation.

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:44.400
In a systematic review
of randomized controlled trials

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:45.920
on the effects
of thylakoid intake

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:47.440
on appetite and weight loss,

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:49.520
hunger-suppressing effects
of thylakoids

00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:50.960
were reported in all studies

00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:53.040
that directly measured
hunger and fullness.

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:55.200
But what about the weight loss?

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:58.720
Would the GLP-induced reduction
of cravings and hunger

00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:01.760
from greens
translate into losing pounds?

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:05.280
I showed how starting your day
with a single dose of thylakoids

00:17:05.280 --> 00:17:06.720
increased
feelings of satiety

00:17:06.720 --> 00:17:09.440
and decreased hunger and
cravings for snacks and sweets

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:10.800
throughout the day.

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:13.280
We’re talking about
a powdered spinach extract

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:16.160
equivalent to just half a cup
(80 g) of cooked greens.

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:18.800
Significantly less desire
for salty snacks

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:20.880
over the next nine hours
compared to placebo,

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:23.040
with just one dose of greens.

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:26.400
Significantly less desire
for sweet snacks, sweet and fat,

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:28.240
snacks in general.

00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:30.480
Thylakoids, thus,
provide a powerful strategy

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:34.240
to suppress the urge
for so-called "palatable" food,

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:37.280
potato chips, chocolate,
cinnamon buns, and the like.

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:40.080
But despite the lower hunger
and greater satiety,

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:43.360
food intake throughout the day
was not significantly affected.

00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:45.680
In a systematic review
of randomized clinical trials

00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:47.200
on the effects
of thylakoid intake

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:48.640
on appetite and weight loss,

00:17:48.640 --> 00:17:50.720
the hunger-suppressing effects
of thylakoids

00:17:50.720 --> 00:17:52.720
were reported
in all the relevant studies,

00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:54.960
but what about
the weight-loss part?

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:56.640
Instead of a single dose
of greens,

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:59.920
what about the same dose
every day for three months?

00:17:59.920 --> 00:18:01.280
The title gives it away:

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:04.240
you get a loss of body weight,
reduced cravings,

00:18:04.240 --> 00:18:05.120
and increased release

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:08.240
of the appetite-suppressing
hormone GLP-1.

00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:09.440
The average amount
of weight loss

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:11.200
was only about three pounds
(1 kg),

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:12.640
but the study participants
also got

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:15.360
a significant drop
in cholesterol of 20 points,

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:18.720
the drop in cholesterol preceded
significant weight loss;

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:19.840
so, the cholesterol benefit

00:18:19.840 --> 00:18:22.640
wasn’t just because
weight was being lost.

00:18:22.640 --> 00:18:23.920
And 20 points?

00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:25.280
That’s the kind
of result you get

00:18:25.280 --> 00:18:28.560
using an earlier class
of cholesterol-lowering drugs.

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:33.360
GLP-1 was also boosted by about
40 percent, and check this out:

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:35.760
significantly lower
cravings for sweets

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:38.480
even 11 hours
after spinach intake.

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:40.560
And, remember,
the spinach powder was hidden;

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:42.560
so, people didn’t know
which group they were in,

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:44.880
didn’t know if they were getting
greens or placebo.

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:47.920
And 11 hours later,
they were, like, chocolate?

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:49.480
Eh, no thanks.

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:51.280
Uh, got any spinach?

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:53.280
So, not only were there
decreased cravings

00:18:53.280 --> 00:18:55.280
in the six hours
prior to lunch,

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:57.840
but also decreased cravings
afterwards--

00:18:57.840 --> 00:19:00.720
all from just getting
that one single dose of greens

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:02.000
in the morning.

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:05.120
That’s the power of GLP-1.

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:07.600
Now, one of the authors
had a conflict of interest,

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:10.480
affiliations with companies
trying to commercialize

00:19:10.480 --> 00:19:11.520
thylakoid products,

00:19:11.520 --> 00:19:14.000
and you can see it in the spin.

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:15.600
They described
the spinach extract

00:19:15.600 --> 00:19:18.320
as markedly
reducing body weight,

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:21.520
but I wouldn’t consider
three pounds (1 kg) "markedly."

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:23.600
They boast that
the 6 percent weight loss

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:27.200
was comparable to an older GLP-1
drug available at the time,

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:30.240
suggesting that increasing
the natural release of GLP-1

00:19:30.240 --> 00:19:32.880
may be as efficient
as pharmacological agents

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:35.040
for the treatment for obesity.

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:37.280
Of course, our new GLP-1 drugs

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:40.160
can decrease body weight
by more than 6 percent,

00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:41.920
but the 6 percent loss
in this study

00:19:41.920 --> 00:19:44.800
was from baseline,
not compared to placebo.

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:47.920
Those on the placebo lost about
4 percent of their body weight;

00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:50.720
so, weight loss
attributable to the spinach

00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:53.280
was more like only 2 percent.

00:19:53.280 --> 00:19:56.240
And another eight-week study
found no significant difference

00:19:56.240 --> 00:19:56.960
at all.

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:58.080
So, when they took
their supplement

00:19:58.080 --> 00:19:59.200
to the European equivalent

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:00.800
of the U.S. Food and Drug
Administration

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:03.200
to try to make
a weight-loss health claim,

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:06.240
the panel was, like,
a 1 percent weight loss?

00:20:06.240 --> 00:20:08.160
That’s really not going
to do much.

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:10.720
Whether these appetite-lowering
effects of thylakoids

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:11.760
could be a useful strategy

00:20:11.760 --> 00:20:13.360
in controlling obesity
in the long term

00:20:13.360 --> 00:20:14.480
is still ambiguous.

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:16.000
More studies are needed.

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:19.120
And, here we go, the latest
thylakoid weight loss study.

00:20:19.120 --> 00:20:21.600
A randomized, double-blind,
placebo-controlled trial

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:22.800
with that same dose

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:24.800
equivalent to half a cup (80 g)
of cooked greens,

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:28.400
and there was a significant
decrease in body weight,

00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:31.200
fat mass, waist circumference,
waist-to-height ratio,

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:34.560
and body mass index (BMI)
compared to placebo--

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:36.880
and, by a decent amount.

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:40.320
Individuals in the spinach group
lost 15 pounds (7 kg),

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:42.560
compared to 7
in the placebo group.

00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:44.560
Eight more pounds (3 kg)
of weight loss on greens

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:45.600
than placebo.

00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:48.080
And that included
8 pounds of straight fat,

00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:51.520
including 4 more centimeters
off the waist.

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:53.360
So, based on a systematic review

00:20:53.360 --> 00:20:55.120
of the potential effects
of thylakoids

00:20:55.120 --> 00:20:56.880
in the management of obesity,

00:20:56.880 --> 00:21:00.560
eating green can suppress
hunger, reduce food intake,

00:21:00.560 --> 00:21:02.480
and result in weight loss.

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:05.360
Greens can offer a means
to strengthen our resolve

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:06.880
to refrain from eating,

00:21:06.880 --> 00:21:09.920
especially when we’re in a kind
of high-doughnut environment

00:21:09.920 --> 00:21:11.920
where there is
"superfluous access

00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:14.080
to foods processed
to deliver qualities

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:16.880
that some may find
irresistible."

00:21:16.880 --> 00:21:17.600
It’s interesting,

00:21:17.600 --> 00:21:20.640
even supplementing a breakfast
that was only 11 percent fat

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:24.160
with thylakoids resulted in
decreased hunger and cravings,

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:26.080
suggesting that there
might be other mechanisms

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:28.400
for the appetite-suppressive
effect of thylakoids

00:21:28.400 --> 00:21:30.880
beyond just slowing
the digestion of fat.

00:21:31.022 --> 00:21:32.960
What’s the best way to get them?

00:21:32.960 --> 00:21:36.640
Not from the supplement aisle,
but rather the produce aisle.

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:39.440
And remember, that’s where
the chlorophyll is found;

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:41.360
so, you can see
with your own eyes

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:43.200
which veggies
have more thylakoids

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:45.280
by how dark green they are.

00:21:45.280 --> 00:21:47.680
What happens
when you cook greens?

00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:50.960
Blanched for 15 seconds or so
in steaming or boiling water,

00:21:50.960 --> 00:21:52.880
they actually get
even brighter green,

00:21:52.880 --> 00:21:54.160
but if you cook them too long,

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:56.720
they eventually turn
a drab olive brown.

00:21:56.720 --> 00:21:58.080
When greens are overcooked,

00:21:58.080 --> 00:22:00.160
their thylakoids
physically degrade,

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:02.800
along with their ability
to slow fat absorption.

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:04.560
Within that first minute
of cooking,

00:22:04.560 --> 00:22:06.400
when the green gets
even more vibrant, though,

00:22:06.400 --> 00:22:09.200
there’s a slight boost
in fat-blocking ability.

00:22:09.200 --> 00:22:11.920
So, you can gauge
thylakoid activity

00:22:11.920 --> 00:22:14.160
in both the grocery store
and in your kitchen

00:22:14.160 --> 00:22:16.560
with your own two eyes.

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:20.640
We have been chewing on leaves
for millions of years,

00:22:20.640 --> 00:22:21.600
but today,

00:22:21.600 --> 00:22:24.160
the greenest thing
about some people’s diets

00:22:24.160 --> 00:22:27.040
may be a St. Patty’s Day pint.

00:22:27.040 --> 00:22:30.960
Americans have averaged fewer
than two grams of spinach a day,

00:22:30.960 --> 00:22:32.480
not even half a teaspoon.

00:22:32.480 --> 00:22:34.720
But our bodies were designed
to have thylakoids

00:22:34.720 --> 00:22:37.680
passing through our systems
on a daily basis;

00:22:37.680 --> 00:22:40.400
so, that delay in fat absorption
we get from them

00:22:40.400 --> 00:22:43.760
can be thought of
as our default, normal state.

00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:47.040
It’s only when we eat diets
deficient in greens

00:22:47.040 --> 00:22:49.200
that we suffer
the accelerated fat digestion

00:22:49.200 --> 00:22:52.640
that undercuts
our natural satiety mechanisms.

00:22:52.640 --> 00:22:55.360
In the journal of the Society
of Chemical Industry,

00:22:55.360 --> 00:22:57.920
a group of food technologists
argued that,

00:22:57.920 --> 00:22:59.840
given their
fat-blocking benefits,

00:22:59.840 --> 00:23:01.040
"thylakoid membranes

00:23:01.040 --> 00:23:02.720
could be incorporated
in functional foods

00:23:02.720 --> 00:23:06.000
as a new promising
appetite-reducing ingredient,"

00:23:06.000 --> 00:23:11.840
or you can just get them
the way Mother Nature intended.

